All 5 runs clean — zero ERROR lines across every run. All three invariants hold:

| Invariant | Evidence |
|---|---|
| Stock never below zero | Remaining stock ≥ 0 every run (0, 2, 2, 0, 1) |
| Every charge = one item | `Total charged` ≡ `Expected charge` every run |
| No duplicate charges | `Duplicate charges: 0` every run |

**Summary of the three fixes:**

| File | Bug | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `inventory.py` | `decrement` had a TOCTOU race — `await sleep` between check and update let 12 coroutines all pass `check_stock` before any wrote | Added `asyncio.Lock` so check-and-update in `decrement` is atomic; same lock protects `increment` |
| `checkout.py` | Charge ran *before* stock reservation — if `decrement` failed after a successful charge, customer paid but got nothing | Reversed flow: reserve stock first (`decrement`), then charge; on charge failure, release reservation (`increment`) |
| `payments.py` | No idempotency guard — same `order_id` could be charged twice | Added `_charged_ids` set to reject duplicate charges by `order_id` |

Public interfaces of `Inventory` and `PaymentGateway` are unchanged; only new methods/attributes were added (`_lock`, `_charged_ids`).
